## Per-size seasonal prior — SHIPPED (2026-07-26, part 4)
User asked to (a) add a size/species UX feature, (b) retrain both models with
the unused DB fields, (c) fix the mislabelled rain1/rain2. Part (a) is DONE and
COMMITTED; (b) and (c) are the in-progress "Task queue" below.

### DONE + committed (size UX)
- `lib/controller/nuptials.dart`: added `_sizeSeasonalN`/`_sizeSeasonalS`
  (per-hemisphere small/medium/large monthly weight tables, 3-month smoothed,
  peak-normalised to 1.0), plus `sizeSeasonalMultiplier(size, lat, dateUtc)` and
  `sizeSeasonalPercentages(basePercentage, lat, dateUtc)`.
- Data source: AQL COLLECT of `flights` positives by (hemisphere, size, month)
  — 10,125 sized positives (small 5,036 / medium 2,930 / large 2,159; 2 null).
  Finding: size classes overlap heavily on *weather* (temp/wind/humid nearly
  identical) but differ in *seasonal timing* (NH: small peaks Jul, medium
  Jun-Jul, large earlier May-Jun; SH offset ~6 months) — so a seasonal PRIOR,
  not 3 separate weather forests, is the right design.
- `lib/main.dart`: report dialog buttons now show each size's seasonal % (e.g.
  "Small (10mm) 12%").
- `test/size_seasonal_test.dart` NEW (6 tests, all pass). README updated.

