### DB schema notes (verified 2026-07-26)
- `flights.weather` = {lat, lon, timezone, daily[8]} (today + 7-day forecast; NO
  past days). daily[i] keys: clouds, dew_point, dt, feels_like, humidity,
  moon_phase, moonrise, moonset, pop, pressure, rain, sunrise, sunset, temp
  (day/min/max/night/eve/morn), uvi, weather, wind_deg, wind_gust, wind_speed.
- `historical.weather` = {current, hourly[24] of the flight day only}. hourly[i]
  keys add: visibility; (no rain-amount split, has pop).
- `current.weather` = single OWM current snapshot.
- No pre-flight days are stored anywhere => "change/lead-up" features need an
  external OWM timemachine backfill (future work).

## Guardrails
- Keep first-page load fast: do not re-introduce `await` on
  `initializeService()` or the notification permission before `runApp()`.
- Do not hand-edit the sklite JSON model assets (`assets/*_model.json`) or
  the `lib/models/forest_model.dart` walker by hand; regenerate JSON from the
  notebooks. (The old generated `models/*.dart` score trees are gone.)
- Prefer `git -C` and verify with `flutter analyze` before claiming done.
- `flutter pub upgrade` has been observed to HANG for many minutes
  (stuck resolving git deps). If it does not finish quickly, kill the
  `dart.exe` processes and use `flutter pub get` instead to reconcile
  `pubspec.lock`. Note: `flutter pub get` may print a non-fatal
  Windows error about deleting `windows/flutter/ephemeral/.plugin_symlinks`
  — that is a desktop-build dir permission quirk and is safe to ignore.
- README.md was expanded (2026-07-18) with features, data flow,
  setup/.env template, and project structure — keep it in sync if you
  add user-facing features or change required API keys.
- Keep the model call-site feature orders in `nuptials.dart` in sync with the
  training notebooks/pipeline. As of the 2026-07-26 retrain the daily model
  uses 15 features and the hourly model uses 12 (both add hemisphere +
  cyclical sin/cos day-of-year + dew-point depression; hourly still has no
  rain/cloud). A mismatched order silently produces wrong predictions.

