### Map shading (2026-07-26, lib/view/map.dart)
The three OWM weather overlays are recoloured via `ColorFilter.matrix` to show
SUITABILITY per the model's PD distribution: BLUE-GREEN/teal = favourable,
RED = unfavourable. Per-layer opacity is weighted by each feature's PD span
(temp 1.00, wind 0.61, cloud 0.19). Temperature is bidirectional. NB the OWM
temp palette has high red across yellow/orange/red, so favourable green is
GATED on `R-G-B` (only *pure red*/hottest passes; yellow/orange/green/cyan
reject) not `R-B` (which lit green almost everywhere); cold => red via `B-R`.
Favourable green/blue is DAMPED (G=(R-G-B)/2, B=(R-G-B)/5) because green reads
~3x brighter than red at equal alpha — keep it below the red or it dominates. Clouds are faint teal (overcast is weakly
favourable); wind is red (calm has no signal to paint).

